# Line endings are decided here, in the repository, instead of by whatever each
# contributor happens to have in their local git config.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout can be saved back with CRLF and show up on
# someone else's clone as every file modified, which turns a one-line change
# into a full-file diff and makes review pointless.
#
# text=auto: git normalizes text files to LF when storing them, and converts on
# checkout to whatever the platform expects.
* text=auto

# Belt and braces for anything that must never be touched by that conversion.
# None of these are in the repository today, but wiring photos and datasheets
# are the obvious thing to add later, and a corrupted binary is a confusing
# failure to debug.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.bin  binary
*.elf  binary
